# Trust anchor for kiban's release-tag signature verification.
#
# git's native `allowed_signers` format (see ssh-keygen(1), VERIFICATION AND ADDING
# SIGNATURES): "<principal> <key-type> <base64-key> [comment]". `lib/self_update.sh`
# passes this file to `git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=... verify-tag` before it will
# fast-forward to (unpinned) or check out (pinned) a release tag.
#
# The principal below must match the `user.email` used when the release tag was
# created (.github/workflows/release.yml) -- that is what git's ssh verification
# matches against, not an arbitrary label.
#
# Rotating this key: add the new key on a new line, signed by a still-trusted key
# under the OLD allowed_signers (self_update.sh reads this file from the working tree
# as it stands *before* applying an update, so the new key only takes effect once a
# release signed under the current trust anchor is accepted). Never remove the last
# working line without a verified replacement already in place -- that locks out every
# clone's unpinned update path until fixed by hand.
release@kiban ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIEX7hbFoETZ6qZeKK+wYiBJk6FLk2iW7N4R7yrBbCJ/X kiban-release-signing
